{"data": {"content": "Fix the software issue described below in the current repository. Inspect the implementation before editing, make the smallest correct change, and run relevant visible tests. Do not inspect benchmark metadata, git history, or hidden evaluation assets. When the patch is ready, give a concise summary.\n\nIssue:\nOLE object icon rId returns incorrect value\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen creating OLE objects with icons, the relationship ID (rId) for the icon image is being returned incorrectly. The method `_icon_rId` is appending an extra \"1\" to the relationship ID, causing issues with icon display.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom pptx.shapes.shapetree import _OleObjectElementCreator\n\n# Mock the slide part to return a specific rId\nclass MockSlidePart:\n    def get_or_add_image_part(self, image_file):\n        return (None, 'rId16')\n\n# Create an OLE object element creator\nelement_creator = _OleObjectElementCreator(None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None)\nelement_creator._slide_part = MockSlidePart()\nelement_creator._icon_image_file = 'obj-icon.emf'\n\n# Get the icon rId\nrId = element_creator._icon_rId\nprint(f\"Expected: rId16\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {rId}\")\n```\n\nThe expected output should be `rId16` but instead returns `rId161`.", "session_id": "scanny__python-pptx_278b47b1_func_basic__pz4s6nc1", "source": "user", "turn_id": "turn-0001"}, "kind": "input", "seq": 1, "time": 1788431641.68911}
